summary: Fuzz sysfs entries related to resource scaling risk assessment.
description: |
  Confirm system call fuzz testing is being performed on cpu, regulator, thermal and cpuidle sysfs entries specified in resource scaling risk assessment.
  The database is checked at the end to ensure each entry was executed at least once.
  Default runtime is 1 hour (3600 seconds), but can be changed using the "timer" parameter.
  Test inputs:
      A list with the sysfs entries to be fuzzed, and a fuzzer program
      called syzkaller. Input details:
      - sysfs entries list from RA documentation.
      - syzkaller code: https://github.com/google/syzkaller
      - check for execution: grep -q "^${syscall}[$,(]" "${local_dir}"/corpus_dir/*
  Expected results:
      If the system calls are executed without incident during the test runtime,
      the following output should be expected:
        [   LOG    ] :: Test duration was 3602 seconds.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index0_level executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index0_level executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index0_shared_cpu_list executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index0_shared_cpu_list executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index0_shared_cpu_map executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index0_shared_cpu_map executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index0_type executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index0_type executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index0_uevent executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index0_uevent executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: openat$cpu0_cache_index1_level executed.
        [   PASS   ] :: write$cpu0_cache_index1_level executed.
